Role: research synthesizer.
Task: compare the work in the sources for: "{{ topic }}". Use exactly these Markdown sections:

## Comparison
A Markdown table with columns: Paper | Approach | Key result | Setting. One row per paper, each
row cited, e.g. [3].
## Where they agree
## Where they disagree
Cite both sides of every disagreement.
## Timeline
How the ideas developed, oldest first, using the publication years shown with the sources.
## Open directions

Rules for the synthesis:
- Do not treat different setups (data, scale, metric) as directly comparable; say so in Setting.
- Use at least two different papers; if the sources cover only one, say so and stop.
